## Lore

The detective character is steeped in the criminal sciences and in investigative
technique. Yet the sleuth is more than a simple detective: he has an uncanny eye
for detail and a mind as sharp and quick as a computer. His daring sense of
adventure will plunge him into a den of thieves or a corporate headquarters,
cloaked in one of his many disguises, and he will stop at little to prove a
theory, play out a hunch or secure a clue.

The character has no special powers and no gimmicks. His special abilities are
skills and cunning, sometimes supported by a handful of cold steel and bullets.
He craves a good challenge as much as he craves adventure, and loves nothing
more than to match wits with the criminal elite.

He is a brain, but far too curious about too many things to have ever taken a
degree - though he has probably had years of college. Only the skills that help
his investigative work have had his full attention: a jack of all trades, and
master of, well, a few.

## GM Notes

**The detective list**, printed 161 - seven of the fourteen, with the one-time
bonus the book prints beside each:

Chemistry (+30%); Chemistry: Analytical (+25%); Criminal Sciences/Forensics
(+30%); Cryptography (+30%); Disguise (+25%); Forgery (+10%); Intelligence
(+20%); Interrogation (+25%); Impersonation (+30%); Paramedic (+25%); Pathology
(+25%); Pick Locks (+20%); Surveillance Systems (+30%); Basic Electronics (+25%).

**The equipment budget**, printed 161: 01-15 $8,000; 16-29 $10,000; 30-45
$12,000; 46-60 $14,000; 61-75 $16,000; 76-89 $18,000; 90-00 $20,000. At least
40% must go on investigative equipment - listening devices, cameras, optics,
sensors - 20% on weapons and related equipment and 20% on other items for
detective work; up to 20% may be saved.

The character has presumably already spent **2D4x10,000 dollars** equipping a
crime lab: microscopes, light-boards, magnifying glasses and jeweller''s lenses,
a chemical analysis bench, a darkroom, a refrigerator unit, electrical
facilities and tape recorders.

**Computer hacking penalties**, printed 161: -10% for a simple security program
(1D6 minutes); -20% moderately sophisticated (4D6 minutes); -40% sophisticated
(3D6 hours); -50% super sophisticated (6D6 hours); -60% a superior military
program (3D4 days); -10% to decipher an unknown data code.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'hu-super-sleuth');


